    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93416" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾰτρᾰπ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a satrap, exercise the authority of one</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖ τὴν γυναῖκα σατραπεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.1.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				302
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PEleph.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξατραπ-</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σατράπης</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen., <i>rule as a
				satrap</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῆς χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.1.10
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.</u>
				3.4.31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Them.</u>
				30
			</span></i>: also c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐν μέσῳ
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.7.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴγυπτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					2.24
				</span></i>
			: metaph. in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				1.27
			</span></i>.</div>
